4. Project Story for Interviews

I built an end-to-end Healthcare Data Warehouse using Python,
Snowflake, dbt and Power BI.

I generated realistic healthcare source data for patients,
doctors, hospitals, appointments, prescriptions and insurance.

The source data intentionally contained data-quality issues such
as missing values, duplicates, invalid values, inconsistent
formats, invalid phone numbers, negative values and future dates.

I loaded the raw data into Snowflake and used dbt to create
staging, intermediate and mart layers.

The final warehouse follows a star schema with fact tables for
appointments, prescriptions and insurance, and dimension tables
for patients, doctors, hospitals and dates.

I implemented data-quality tests including uniqueness,
not-null validation and referential-integrity checks.

For security, I implemented Snowflake RBAC, masking policies,
row access policies and secure views conceptually.

Finally, I connected the mart layer to Power BI and created
executive, patient, doctor, hospital, insurance and prescription
analytics dashboards.











